  "generated_text": "1. The center of the circle is the midpoint of the diameter.\n2. The midpoint formula for two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\left( \\frac{x_1 + x_2}{2}, \\frac{y_1 + y_2}{2} \\right)\n   \\]\n3. Substitute the given endpoints \\((-1, -4)\\) and \\((-7, 6)\\) into the midpoint formula:\n   \\[\n   \\left( \\frac{-1 + (-7)}{2}, \\frac{-4 + 6}{2} \\right)\n   \\]\n4. Simplify the expressions:\n   \\[\n   \\left( \\frac{-1 - 7}{2}, \\frac{-4 + 6}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{-8}{2}, \\frac{2}{2} \\right) = \\left( -4, 1 \\right)\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the center of circle \\(M\\) are \\(\\boxed{(-4,1)}\\).",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[Interval.open(-4, 1), '(-4,1)']",
    "gold_answer": "The midpoint of a diameter of a circle is its center. Thus, $M$ is the midpoint of the segment from $(-1,-4)$ to $(-7,6),$ so $M$ has coordinates \\[\\left(\\frac{-1+(-7)}{2},\\frac{-4+6}{2} \\right)=\\boxed{(-4,1)}.\\]",
    "is_correct": true
  },
